.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt PQCAP-ENTER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pqcap-enter
.Nd enter capability mode, then exec (T18, T20)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -root Ar dir
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Limits stdio with
.Fn caph_limit_stdio ,
enters capability mode with
.Fn caph_enter ,
then
.Fn execvp
the command.
.Pp
If
.Fl -root
is given, that directory is opened
.Em before
enter, rights-limited
.Pq lookup, read, write, create, fchdir, … ,
duplicated onto fd 3, and exported as
.Ev PQCAP_ROOTFD .
The child must use
.Fn openat
on that fd.
.Fn namei
of a new path is the TOCTOU this wrapper closes.
.Pp
FreeBSD only. GENERIC already has Capsicum; this is not a
.Xr kldload 8 .
Not Casper.
Not
.Xr mac 4 .
Do not wrap
.Nm sshd
or
.Nm login .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PQCAP_ROOTFD
.It Ev PQCAP_ROOTFD
Set to
.Ql 3
when
.Fl -root
is used.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr openat 2 ,
.Xr caph_enter 3 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr freebsd-capsicum 7
.Sh AUTHORS
Brian Fundakowski Feldman.
Capsicum is Watson, Anderson, Laurie, Kennaway, USENIX Security 2010.
